{"subjectId":"python","id":"files-io","title":"Files & pathlib","group":"Errors, Modules & Files","order":49,"html":"<p class=\"lead\">Reading and writing files safely with <code>with</code>, text vs binary modes, seeking and chunked reads, <code>pathlib</code> for paths, and <code>shutil</code> / <code>tempfile</code> for everything around them.</p>\n<section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-file\"></i>Text files</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>import os, tempfile\npath = os.path.join(tempfile.mkdtemp(), \"notes.txt\")\n\nwith open(path, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:     # \"w\" truncates, \"a\" appends\n    f.write(\"line one\\nline two\\n\")\n\nwith open(path, encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:           # default mode \"r\"\n    for line in f:                                # streams line by line\n        print(line.rstrip())</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>line one\nline two</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Mode</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>'r'</code></td><td>Read (default) — error if missing</td></tr><tr><td><code>'w'</code></td><td>Write — creates or <strong>truncates</strong></td></tr><tr><td><code>'a'</code></td><td>Append to the end</td></tr><tr><td><code>'x'</code></td><td>Create — error if it exists</td></tr><tr><td><code>'b'</code></td><td>Binary, e.g. <code>'rb'</code> for images</td></tr><tr><td><code>'+'</code></td><td>Read and write</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<div class=\"callout callout--warn\"><div class=\"callout-label\">Watch out</div><p>Always pass <code>encoding=\"utf-8\"</code> for text — the platform default differs between Windows and macOS/Linux.</p></div>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-book\"></i>Reading methods</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>import io\nf = io.StringIO(\"alpha\\nbeta\\ngamma\\n\")    # behaves like an open text file\n\nprint(f.readline())            # alpha\nprint(f.read(3))               # bet\nprint(f.readlines())           # ['a\\n', 'gamma\\n']\nprint(repr(f.read()))          # ''   ← at the end, read() returns an empty string</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>alpha\n\nbet\n['a\\n', 'gamma\\n']\n''</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Call</th><th>Returns</th><th>Memory</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>for line in f</code></td><td>One line at a time</td><td>O(1) — best for big files</td></tr><tr><td><code>f.read()</code></td><td>The whole file as one string</td><td>Whole file</td></tr><tr><td><code>f.read(n)</code></td><td>Up to <code>n</code> characters (bytes in binary mode)</td><td>O(n)</td></tr><tr><td><code>f.readline()</code></td><td>Next line, including <code>\\n</code></td><td>One line</td></tr><tr><td><code>f.readlines()</code></td><td>List of all lines</td><td>Whole file</td></tr><tr><td><code>f.write(s)</code> / <code>f.writelines(lines)</code></td><td>Write text (no newline added)</td><td>—</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-binary\"></i>Binary files, chunks &amp; seek/tell</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>import os, tempfile\npath = os.path.join(tempfile.mkdtemp(), \"data.bin\")\n\nwith open(path, \"wb\") as f:\n    f.write(bytes(range(10)))\n\nchunks = []\nwith open(path, \"rb\") as f:\n    while chunk := f.read(4):             # fixed-size chunks: constant memory\n        chunks.append(chunk)\nprint(chunks)                             # [b'\\x00\\x01\\x02\\x03', b'\\x04\\x05\\x06\\x07', b'\\x08\\t']\n\nwith open(path, \"rb\") as f:\n    f.seek(6)                             # jump to byte offset 6\n    print(f.tell(), f.read(2))            # 6 b'\\x06\\x07'\n    f.seek(-1, os.SEEK_END)               # 1 byte before the end\n    print(f.read())                       # b'\\t'</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"callout callout--note\"><div class=\"callout-label\">Key point</div><p>In text mode, <code>seek</code> only accepts offsets previously returned by <code>tell()</code> (or 0) because characters can be several bytes. Use binary mode for random access. Hashing a big file? Read it in chunks and call <code>h.update(chunk)</code>.</p></div>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-clock\"></i>Temporary files &amp; directories</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>import os, tempfile\n\nwith tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as d:          # deleted with everything inside\n    path = os.path.join(d, \"scratch.txt\")\n    with open(path, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n        f.write(\"draft\")\n    print(os.path.exists(path))                   # True\nprint(os.path.exists(d))                          # False\n\nwith tempfile.NamedTemporaryFile(\"w+\", suffix=\".txt\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as tmp:\n    tmp.write(\"scratch\")\n    tmp.seek(0)                                   # rewind before reading back\n    print(tmp.read(), tmp.name.endswith(\".txt\"))  # scratch True</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-folder\"></i>pathlib</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>from pathlib import Path\nimport tempfile\n\nroot = Path(tempfile.mkdtemp())\nreport = root / \"reports\" / \"2026.txt\"      # \"/\" joins paths\nreport.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\nreport.write_text(\"ok\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n\nprint(report.name, report.stem, report.suffix)   # 2026.txt 2026 .txt\nprint(report.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))         # ok\nprint([p.name for p in root.rglob(\"*.txt\")])      # ['2026.txt']\nprint(report.relative_to(root).as_posix())        # reports/2026.txt\nprint(report.with_suffix(\".md\").name)             # 2026.md</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Task</th><th><code>os</code> / <code>os.path</code></th><th><code>pathlib</code></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Join</td><td><code>os.path.join(a, b)</code></td><td><code>Path(a) / b</code></td></tr><tr><td>File name / extension</td><td><code>os.path.basename(p)</code>, <code>os.path.splitext(p)</code></td><td><code>p.name</code>, <code>p.stem</code>, <code>p.suffix</code></td></tr><tr><td>Parent folder</td><td><code>os.path.dirname(p)</code></td><td><code>p.parent</code></td></tr><tr><td>Exists / is file</td><td><code>os.path.exists(p)</code>, <code>os.path.isfile(p)</code></td><td><code>p.exists()</code>, <code>p.is_file()</code></td></tr><tr><td>Make folders</td><td><code>os.makedirs(p, exist_ok=True)</code></td><td><code>p.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)</code></td></tr><tr><td>List / pattern match</td><td><code>os.listdir(p)</code>, <code>glob.glob('*.py')</code></td><td><code>p.iterdir()</code>, <code>p.glob('*.py')</code>, <code>p.rglob('*.py')</code></td></tr><tr><td>Read whole file</td><td><code>open(p).read()</code></td><td><code>p.read_text(encoding=…)</code>, <code>p.read_bytes()</code></td></tr><tr><td>Absolute path</td><td><code>os.path.abspath(p)</code></td><td><code>p.resolve()</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<div class=\"callout callout--note\"><div class=\"callout-label\">Key point</div><p>Prefer <code>pathlib</code> in new code — paths become objects with methods instead of strings passed to functions. Every standard-library function that takes a path also accepts a <code>Path</code>.</p></div>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-copy\"></i>glob &amp; shutil: finding, copying, moving</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>import glob, os, shutil, tempfile\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nwith tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as d:\n    root = Path(d)\n    for name in [\"a.py\", \"b.py\", \"notes.md\"]:\n        (root / name).write_text(name, encoding=\"utf-8\")\n\n    print(sorted(p.name for p in root.glob(\"*.py\")))                          # ['a.py', 'b.py']\n    print(sorted(os.path.basename(p) for p in glob.glob(str(root / \"*.md\"))))  # ['notes.md']\n\n    backup = root / \"backup\"\n    backup.mkdir()\n    shutil.copy(root / \"a.py\", backup)                  # copy into a folder\n    shutil.move(root / \"notes.md\", backup / \"README.md\")  # move + rename\n    print(sorted(p.name for p in backup.iterdir()))     # ['README.md', 'a.py']\n\n    shutil.rmtree(backup)                               # delete a whole tree\n    print(backup.exists())                              # False</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-shield-check\"></i>Safe writes</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>import os, tempfile\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\ndef atomic_write(path: Path, text: str) -&gt; None:\n    \"\"\"Readers see either the old file or the new one — never half a file.\"\"\"\n    tmp = path.with_suffix(path.suffix + \".tmp\")\n    tmp.write_text(text, encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    os.replace(tmp, path)            # atomic rename on the same filesystem\n\ntarget = Path(tempfile.mkdtemp()) / \"settings.json\"\natomic_write(target, '{\"theme\": \"dark\"}')\nprint(target.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))   # {\"theme\": \"dark\"}</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"grid\"><div class=\"callout callout--good\"><div class=\"callout-label\">Do</div><p>Use <code>with open(...)</code>, pass <code>encoding=\"utf-8\"</code>, stream big files line by line or in chunks, and use <code>tempfile</code> for scratch files.</p></div><div class=\"callout callout--bad\"><div class=\"callout-label\">Avoid</div><p>Calling <code>open()</code> without closing it, <code>read()</code> on multi-GB files, or building paths with string <code>+</code> (<code>folder + \"/\" + name</code>).</p></div></div>\n<p>Structured formats — JSON, CSV, pickle, TOML — are covered in <strong>Serialization: JSON, CSV &amp; pickle</strong>.</p>\n<details class=\"qa\"><summary>How would you process a 10 GB log file?</summary><div><p>Stream it: <code>with open(path, encoding='utf-8') as f: for line in f:</code> keeps one line in memory at a time. For binary data read fixed-size chunks with <code>f.read(1 &lt;&lt; 20)</code>. Combine with generators to build a lazy pipeline.</p></div></details></section>"}